			<div class="content" id="post-content-1535329">
									

<p>A few other things I noticed.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>interest grows</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Interest is not an objectively measurable quantity.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>ANY attempt</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The capital letters are inappropriate. And you're not advertising the book, you don't need to emphasise.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>will NOT notice</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Same issue here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>disturbing</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You're sort of on the border here of this being incorrect. While it's a subjective assertion made in an objective document, although you do note it as being a report from another party. From a creative writing standpoint, however, it's bad. Show, don't tell.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>annoying loudmouth guests.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>turn into instructions for disturbing rituals</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>bizarre alterations</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>things as simple</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>perfect meatloaf</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is not on the border. These are, quite definitely, unjustified subjective assertions.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;The quality of our annual office Christmas Party has really gone up since testing on this SCP began&quot; Dr. ████████</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd reccomend you excise this whole bit.</p>

